x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 constructors here and calls them directly, where cxx1 emits C1 and C2 as it does everywhere. Measured, and it is about `inline` rather than about moves: every constructor in this case is defined inside the class body, and writing the same three out of line makes clang emit C1 and C2 on this target too - as it already does for by-value.cpp, which is why no earlier case met this. arm64-darwin emits both either way and agrees with cxx1 on all 8 names, so the mangling is not in question; what differs is which of two identical variants clang bothers to emit for a linkonce_odr constructor on ELF. cxx1's extra C1 is a superset and the case links and runs.
